meta {
  name: Read the audit trail
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{host}}/audit-events?pageNumber=1&pageSize=20
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  200. The business trail, newest first: what changed, to which entity, at whose hand, when,
  and under which request.

  Read-only by design. There is no endpoint that writes, edits or deletes an entry, and the
  entries themselves are written inside the transaction of the change they describe - so a
  loan exists if and only if the trail records it.

  Refusals are not here. The trail says what the library did; an attempt that changed no
  state is a log line, and it is logged.

  Filters: entityType (book, user, loan), entityId, action, actor, correlationId, from, to.
  An unknown entityType is a 400 rather than an empty page.
}
